{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2745","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2745","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2745\",\"parent_revision\":\"37c79f0180a6070d431c4667b8d331ed845f0696b9d33ac350fe5b8b5364d9d8\",\"root_revision\":\"37c79f0180a6070d431c4667b8d331ed845f0696b9d33ac350fe5b8b5364d9d8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nwork-backlog-item process docs read backlog fields/sections that the GitHub-backend groomer doesn't actually populate under those names, forcing manual fallbacks. Observed twice while working #2658: (1) groom-check.md and prepare.md Step 3.1 staleness check reads a top-level groomed date field from backlog_view() output to decide whether an item is groomed or stale; calling backlog_view for #2658 returned an empty groomed field even though the item carried a full Groomed (2026-06-20) section with real grooming content (Impact, Resources, RT-ICA Assessment). The field the doc names is never populated for GitHub-backend items, so the only way to detect groom staleness was to parse the section header date manually. (2) groom-check.md and feasibility-gate.md both name an impact radius section (with a resources section as documented fallback) as the field to read for blast-radius and staleness file-list extraction; calling backlog_view for #2658 with full detail showed the item sections were named Impact and Resources, not Impact Radius, so the primary-key lookup always misses and falls through to the fallback path. Both mismatches will recur on every GitHub-backend item because they stem from a schema naming drift between what these process docs expect and what the actual grooming template plus GitHub backend produce.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Needed fix: audit the groomer's actual output field and section names against every place in the work-backlog-item reference docs that reads them by name (groom-check.md, prepare.md, feasibility-gate.md, rt-ica-gate.md, and any others), and either update the process docs to read the real names produced, or update the groomer to populate the names the docs expect, whichever is the more durable single source of truth, so the fallback parsing workaround is no longer required.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **work-backlog-item process docs reference stale field/section names not produced by github-backend grooming** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - discovered while working backlog item #2658\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-07-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7c1103931728f54a2d03af8cb174cb39fa1937e4031124950745515e6232dbe8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrYeA\"}"}